Finding: {"title":"Journal idx numbers do not match their SQL filename's numeric prefix for two entries (0089/0091 swapped) — no guard rail catches this class of drift","severity":"MEDIUM","area":"data-layer / migration ordering integrity","files":["drizzle/meta/_journal.json","drizzle/0089_add_stage_check_tables.sql","drizzle/0091_add_workflow_canvas_fields.sql",".husky/pre-push"],"detail":"In drizzle/meta/_journal.json, journal idx 89 maps to tag `0091_add_workflow_canvas_fields` and idx 91 maps to tag `0089_add_stage_check_tables` — the idx field and the filename's own numeric prefix disagree for these two entries. This is the same class of ordering corruption that produced multiple emergency repair blocks in scripts/db-migrate.ts (e.g. the 0075/0174, 0079/0080, 0132/0133 timestamp-skip blocks address symptoms of out-of-order/mismatched journal entries). The pre-push hook has orphan-file, orphan-snapshot, and cross-branch index-conflict checks, but nothing validates a journal entry's idx matches its own tag's numeric filename prefix.","impact":"drizzle-orm applies migrations in journal-array order (not filename-prefix order), gated on `when` timestamp vs the tracking table's max created_at. A human skimming drizzle/*.sql filenames to reason about apply order will draw the wrong conclusion for this pair. Low blast radius today (both entries are already tracked/applied everywhere per the repair-probe history), but a landmine for the next person diagnosing an out-of-order migration bug.","recommendation":"Add a cheap static check (alongside the existing `drizzle-kit check` step) asserting `entry.idx === parseInt(entry.tag.split('_')[0], 10)` for every journal entry. Fix these two entries if renumbering is judged safe, or document the known exception if renumbering churn isn't worth it (both are fully applied everywhere already).","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.
